REGEDIT4

; Wine drivers and services a TV has no use for (build/make-prefix.sh, and
; wine-tv once for older prefixes). Wine's device manager loads drivers for
; the devices listed under Enum\ROOT\WINE whatever the service's Start value
; says, so the device entries themselves go: Bluetooth (winebth, which failed
; to start on every launch), USB passthrough (wineusb), and HID/game
; controllers (winebus, built without its input backends here). One fewer
; winedevice.exe. The event log's svchost.exe then starts only on demand.

[-HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\System\CurrentControlSet\Enum\ROOT\WINE\WINEBTH]
[-HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\System\CurrentControlSet\Enum\ROOT\WINE\WINEBUS]
[-HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\System\CurrentControlSet\Enum\ROOT\WINE\WINEUSB]

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\System\CurrentControlSet\Services\Eventlog]
"Start"=dword:00000003
